{"name":"Greystoke","hex":"#85837e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Greystoke","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A village and civil parish in Westmorland and Furness, Cumbria, England, previously in Eden district ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Greystoke"}],"entries":[{"title":"Greystoke, Cumbria","blocks":[{"text":"Greystoke is a village and civil parish on the edge of the Lake District National Park in Cumbria, England, about 4 miles (6.4 km) west of Penrith. At the 2001 census the parish had a population of 642, increasing marginally to 654 at the 2011 Census. The village centres on a green surrounded by stone houses and cottages."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/St_Andrew%27s%2C_Greystoke_-_geograph.org.uk_-_996393.jpg/330px-St_Andrew%27s%2C_Greystoke_-_geograph.org.uk_-_996393.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greystoke%2C_Cumbria","wikidata":"Q3243128"},{"title":"Greystoke Castle","blocks":[{"text":"Greystoke Castle is in the village of Greystoke 8 kilometres (5.0 mi) west of Penrith in the county of Cumbria in northern England.. It is owned by the Howard family and is a private residence including a castle and family estate with no public access."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Greystoke_Castle.jpg/330px-Greystoke_Castle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greystoke_Castle","wikidata":"Q5608483"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Fort_Putnam%2C_Greystoke_-_geograph.org.uk_-_81221.jpg/120px-Fort_Putnam%2C_Greystoke_-_geograph.org.uk_-_81221.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Fort_Putnam%2C_Greystoke_-_geograph.org.uk_-_81221.jpg/250px-